Subject: [PATCH] hyprvx: dev-only camera control (HYPRVX_DEV)

Patch 0005 of the HyprVX V3 series (Feature 001, Sprint 1), per
contracts/dev-control.md v1.1.

- CMake option HYPRVX_DEV (default OFF) defines HYPRVX_DEV; without it
  DevControl.cpp compiles to an empty registerDevControl().
- Dispatchers hyprvx-dev:camera <Px> <Py> <z> (focused monitor),
  hyprvx-dev:camera-mon <monitor> <Px> <Py> <z>, hyprvx-dev:panic,
  hyprvx-dev:state and hyprvx-dev:full-damage. Values go through
  HyprVX::setCamera, i.e. cammath::validate; rejection replies
  err:invalid (unknown monitor: err:monitor) and leaves the camera
  unchanged. panic resets every camera to exact identity and never
  fails.
- `hyprctl hyprvx-dev <command> [args]` runs the same handlers with
  either config parser and returns the state JSON for `state`
  (dispatch replies are only ok/error).
- SMonitorCamera counts the camera hint elements added to render
  passes (passElementsAdded; identity must add none).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
